Z||000000||mrfixit58||08-04-2000||11:23 AM||||Can any one tell me if the stock amp for the sub-woofer is a full frequency amplifier or is there a built in band pass filter that limits it to only the low frequency?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||286SE'S||08-04-2000||01:12 PM||||According to the schematic, it sums the output of all four speakers to a low pass filter. It has 20 watts of power but I doubt that is RMS power from the components used. It is more likely about 7-10 watts. The 1986 Pontiac firebird uses the same amp to drive 2 of the 5 1/2" woofers (one on each side of the rear seats) Hope this helps you.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||08-04-2000||02:16 PM||||Maybe this site will help <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/sub.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/sub.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||08-05-2000||10:23 AM||||286SE's,<P>Have you looked at the schematics and seen if there is a way to by-pass the low pass filter? The reason I ask is I was thinking about using one a couple of exta amps I'v collected to drive better speakers. Kinda like the Bose system. Ya think it'll work?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
